report.summary:
The learner interface in INTERFACE_CONTRACTS section 11 is implemented in crucible/src/crucible/experience/. Of the 22 L requirements, 18 pass on this branch. S.2, S.3, S.5 and SP-11.1 fail on purpose because the v5 Tier 2 domains, Tier 3 civilisations and semantic encoders have not been merged yet.

What works:
- **One interface and one constructor.** `make(tier, name, seed, reward_mode)` returns an `ExperienceEnv` with the 15-field Observation. Numbers are exact (money in integer cents) and events are never silently truncated. Every event caused by an agent's own action carries a `cause` (which action, when, how long after), and `execute` returns the matching `action_seq`.
- **Tier 1 adapter (`MechExperienceEnv`).** It wraps the 4.0 MechVecEnv/SelfPlayEnv and uses the kernel facility's own `rig.*` and `bank.accounts` tools and principals. Specs, reports and balances match the kernel twin tick for tick.
- **Kernel adapter (`KernelExperienceEnv`).** It works on any WorldSpec with several agents. It covers tool discovery with 13 tool categories, artifacts, entities, resources, public analytics, `missing` notes, objectives and an evaluator-side `verify()`.
- **Three reward modes.** They work in the adapters and as a `reward_mode=` keyword on MechVecEnv, KernelMechEnv, SelfPlayEnv, KernelSelfPlayEnv, the Gym and PettingZoo envs, WorldEnv and the CAM 2.0 adapter. Legacy mode is byte-identical to the 4.0 source at c07098b: 11 of 11 runs match.
- **Reward-leakage tests.** 11 explicit tests and 9 planted canaries: zero nonzero rewards in observation-only mode, zero privileged keys, zero canary hits, and observations identical across modes and across evaluator-only data.
- **Other pieces:**
  - an append-only ExperienceStore with per-record hashes, a hash-chained manifest and crash recovery;
  - a ReferenceLearner (159k-parameter recurrent network) with real updates in observation-only mode and exact checkpoints;
  - the `run_learner` loop;
  - parallel worlds via VecExperience and the unchanged RolloutFarm (4 worker processes ran at once);
  - a reproducible CLI (`python -m crucible.experience run`);
  - an admitted `exp` kernel module for self-experiments that returns evidence and pays nothing;
  - scripted reference agents;
  - the LEARNER_GUIDE;
  - an external CAM-shaped adapter that imports only the public interface and changes no environment file.

Measured: S.7 4 parallel environments; S.4 1,140 records stored, then a fresh learner made 18 updates from them; SP-11.2 13 of 13 tool categories; SP-11.5 8 of 8 long-horizon features. The regression run (12 affected 4.0 test files plus 55 earlier) shows 288 passed and 2 skipped. I did not check whether those 2 skips are the 2 in the Gate A baseline.
